athbf{a}) - 2 (\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}) = 3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} - 2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we compute the scalar multiplications:\n\n\\[\n3 \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\n\\[\n-2 \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nAdding these two vectors together, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 14 \\\\ -36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 - 2 \\\\ -21 + 14 \\\\ -6 - 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -14 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -42 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]","id":"precalculus:429"}
